Subject: moddefs.h: a driver may have block rows

The comment on struct mod_drv_data still said character drivers only
and drv_bcount 0; patch 0031 gave pinned drivers block rows, and a
block-only driver (drv_ccount 0) is what C4-2 asks of the ramdisk.
Comment only.

--- a/include/sys/moddefs.h
+++ b/include/sys/moddefs.h
@@ -60,9 +60,10 @@
 };
 
 /*
- * A driver: its switch rows and majors.  Character drivers only, one
- * or more consecutive majors; drv_bcount must be 0.  d_open and
- * d_close of a loaded row stay the loader's trampolines.  A STREAMS
+ * A driver: its switch rows and majors, each one or more consecutive
+ * majors; either count may be 0, not both.  d_open and d_close of a
+ * loaded character row stay the loader's trampolines.  Block rows are
+ * filled when the module links, and need a pinned module.  A STREAMS
  * driver (d_str set) is held from the open that sets q_ptr to the
  * close, as a STREAMS module; its majors are registered MOD_TY_SDEV.
  */
